    details_label: Longer answers
    details:
      - title: How to file a complaint with the Buyer App
        bullets:
          - text: File a complaint with the app / website through which you placed your
              order (hereafter called the "Buyer App"). If you haven’t already
              filed a complaint, you can use the contact details of the Buyer
              Apps from the directory below.
          - text: Upon filing a complaint, the Buyer App will provide you with a ticket
              number for your complaint, and an estimated time to resolve your
              complaint.
          - text: The Buyer App will then work with the seller and other parties to resolve
              your issue within that promised time.
          - text: You may be asked to provide some additional information (such as photos or
              screenshots) in order for your complaint to get resolved quickly.
              So be sure to check your app / email / messages / phone-calls for
              the same.
        body: ''
      - title: How will the Buyer App resolve my complaint?
        bullets:
          - text: When you file a complaint, the Buyer App will first acknowledge your
              complaint, and contact the seller and the platform that the seller
              uses (known as the Seller App), and give you a promised time to
              resolve the complaint. By law (under the E-commerce Rules 2020),
              the Buyer App must provide you with this response within 48 hours
              from you filing the complaint.
          - text: The Buyer App will then work with the seller, Seller App and other parties
              such as the delivery partners, to try to resolve your issue within
              the promised time.
          - text: Typically, in the case of product or delivery related issues, the seller
              or Seller App will be responsible for resolving your complaint,
              while the Buyer App only facilitates the coordination and
              information exchange for complaints resolution.
          - text: If your complaint pertains to a defective / damaged / wrong product or
              deficient service, typically, any refund or replacement that you
              are offered may depend on the seller and/or Seller App and/or
              delivery agent performing their own independent investigation into
              the matter.
          - text: As far as possible, the seller and Seller App will not reach out to you
              directly. All their communication with you will be through the
              Buyer App, unless there is a specific reason for them to contact
              you directly.
          - text: In any case, by law (under the E-commerce Rules 2020), your complaint has
              to be resolved within 30 days from you filing it. So if the Buyer
              App has not communicated a resolution or closure to you within 30
              days, you can escalate the complaint to ONDC.
        body: ''
